WEBVTT

01:30.480 --> 01:36.490
Salvation

01:33.100 --> 01:36.910
I will now reveal the results
 of the ninth vote.

01:36.990 --> 01:40.510
Tetsuzo Sato


 Takayoshi Miura

 Shingo Fujita


 Takahiro Kikuzawa

 Kosuke Tsunoda


 Teruyuki Eda

 Hiroto Kitamura


 Yuji Fukunaga

 Nao Kanzaki

01:37.520 --> 01:40.750
Next, I will reveal the movement of votes.

01:40.510 --> 01:41.490
Nao Kanzaki


 Tetsuzo Sato

 Takayoshi Miura


 Shingo Fujita

 Takahiro Kikuzawa


 Kosuke Tsunoda

 Teruyuki Eda


Hiroto Kitamura

 Yuji Fukunaga

01:44.660 --> 01:47.750
Nao Kanzaki

01:46.570 --> 01:47.750
Wha...

01:47.750 --> 01:49.870
What the hell?!

01:49.870 --> 01:53.880
Hey! What's going on here?!

01:53.880 --> 01:55.170
What do you mean?

01:55.810 --> 01:59.420
I got ten votes from each of you!

02:00.200 --> 02:04.020
Ten votes... from each of us?

02:04.020 --> 02:05.340
Did she get you, too?

02:05.340 --> 02:07.220
You mean she also got you?

02:07.220 --> 02:08.750
For 70 million?

02:08.750 --> 02:10.290
For 70 million, yeah.

02:11.280 --> 02:16.320
Then all that about the highest-scoring
loser having nineteen votes was...

02:16.320 --> 02:18.170
Oh, that was a lie.

02:18.170 --> 02:22.200
I don't actually know if there are 
revival rounds happening elsewhere.

02:22.200 --> 02:24.950
You tricked me!

02:24.950 --> 02:26.590
And what's wrong with that?

02:28.250 --> 02:30.310
This is the Liar Game.

02:30.800 --> 02:32.970
It's all about tricking people.

02:34.020 --> 02:35.080
Right?

02:35.080 --> 02:36.440
When did you...

02:36.440 --> 02:37.970
Wait, are you helping her?!

02:37.970 --> 02:42.060
That's not fair! Outsiders can't 
participate in this game!

02:42.060 --> 02:43.710
Calm down. You've got it all wrong.

02:44.760 --> 02:47.710
Players are allowed to bring 
anything they want into this game.

02:47.710 --> 02:51.220
In other words, I'm one of 
Nao Kanzaki's possessions.

02:53.630 --> 02:55.360
What is wrong with you people?!

02:55.650 --> 02:58.620
How stupid are you, 
giving her your votes?!

02:58.850 --> 03:03.870
How could you not realize she'd say 
the same thing to the other players?

03:04.230 --> 03:06.120
How was I supposed to know that?

03:06.550 --> 03:10.500
She bought my votes with all 
the game money she had left!

03:10.500 --> 03:12.620
Wh-What do you mean?

03:12.620 --> 03:14.860
Kikuzawa-san's right.

03:14.860 --> 03:18.090
I bought his votes with the 
70 million yen I have left.

03:18.530 --> 03:20.310
What about the others?

03:20.310 --> 03:22.490
I bought votes from them the same way.

03:22.490 --> 03:24.970
I promised them all 70 million yen.

03:25.660 --> 03:27.380
Wait a minute here!

03:27.380 --> 03:31.440
You can't overdraw your 
M Ticket ledger like that!

03:31.440 --> 03:32.440
That's right.

03:32.440 --> 03:37.700
So I promised to pay each of the
 other seven players 70 million yen

03:37.700 --> 03:40.570
before the tenth round
in exchange for ten votes.

03:40.570 --> 03:42.070
What?!

03:42.070 --> 03:46.040
You won't be able to afford that!
 That's 100 mil for each breach!

03:46.040 --> 03:48.320
So 600 million for the six 
people you can't pay!

03:48.320 --> 03:50.470
You're the one who ends up in the hole!

03:50.470 --> 03:51.580
I'm aware.

03:51.580 --> 03:55.340
But I'm fairly certain
 I won't have to pay a thing.

03:55.340 --> 03:56.390
What?

03:56.390 --> 03:59.580
Forget about that for now 
and look at the monitor.

03:59.590 --> 04:10.600
Nao Kanzaki


 Tetsuzo Sato

 Takayoshi Miura


 Shingo Fujita

 Takahiro Kikuzawa


 Kosuke Tsunoda

 Teruyuki Eda


Hiroto Kitamura

 Yuji Fukunaga

03:59.930 --> 04:04.400
There are currently eight people here short
of the fifty votes needed to secure a win,

04:04.400 --> 04:08.650
while Nao Kanzaki is thirty votes over.

04:09.150 --> 04:10.610
In light of this...

04:11.090 --> 04:13.730
We're willing to sell off
 those thirty votes.

04:14.990 --> 04:19.350
If you want to win, come tell me 
how much you're willing to pay.

04:20.150 --> 04:22.580
I'll sell to whoever makes the best offer.

04:23.430 --> 04:26.070
Of course, you're under no 
obligation to buy our votes.

04:26.070 --> 04:28.820
You'll just lose the game deep in the red.

04:29.490 --> 04:31.380
You'd better come to terms with it.

04:31.380 --> 04:33.770
The paradigm just shifted.

04:34.330 --> 04:38.960
Nao Kanzaki

04:34.330 --> 04:37.600
The person in full control 
of this game is Nao Kanzaki.

04:38.140 --> 04:44.110
Your lives are completely in our hands.

04:46.760 --> 04:52.890
Takahiro Kikuzawa





 Kosuke Tsunoda




 Teruyuki Eda





 Hiroto Kitamura




 Yuji Fukunaga

04:48.580 --> 04:52.890
Right now, you, Fukunaga, 
and I are tied for last place.

04:53.240 --> 04:56.490
Fukunaga's probably got 
something up her sleeve,

04:56.490 --> 04:59.290
which means one of us is bound to lose.

04:59.290 --> 05:01.900
We'll be another 100 million plus in debt.

05:02.180 --> 05:04.900
There's no way I could ever pay that back.

05:04.900 --> 05:08.020
My life's basically over, I guess.

05:08.380 --> 05:11.010
We'll have to buy those votes.

05:11.010 --> 05:13.050
For how much, though?

05:15.280 --> 05:18.570
We should probably be ready 
to pay at least 10 million.

05:18.920 --> 05:22.300
Ten million? Out of the question.

05:22.640 --> 05:24.680
How much do you want, then?

05:24.680 --> 05:25.800
Let's see...

05:26.130 --> 05:28.550
That'll be at least 70 million.

05:28.550 --> 05:30.620
S-Seventy million?!

05:30.620 --> 05:31.870
Th-That's way too high!

05:31.870 --> 05:33.060
It's not too high at all!

05:33.360 --> 05:35.550
Think about it, gents.

05:35.550 --> 05:39.290
Say you buy the votes for 10 million.

05:35.560 --> 05:37.210
10 million

05:35.560 --> 05:37.210
10 million

05:36.560 --> 05:49.870
-10 million

05:36.560 --> 05:49.870
-10 million

05:37.000 --> 05:49.870
10 million

05:37.000 --> 05:49.870
10 million

05:39.290 --> 05:41.710
We'll take your 10 million

05:41.150 --> 05:46.820
70 million

05:41.150 --> 05:46.820
70 million

05:41.710 --> 05:43.900
but can't repay the 70 million we owe you.

05:43.900 --> 05:45.690
That puts us in breach of contract,

05:45.690 --> 05:48.710
and we have to pay a 100-million-yen 
penalty to the LGT Office.

05:46.900 --> 05:49.870
-100 million

05:46.900 --> 05:49.870
-100 million

05:49.390 --> 05:51.710
Here's what we'll all end up shelling out.

05:49.870 --> 05:52.530
-180 million

05:49.970 --> 05:52.530
-10 million

05:50.140 --> 05:52.530
-10 million

05:52.770 --> 05:56.690
But if you both buy votes 
from us for 70 million,

05:53.160 --> 05:54.850
70 million

05:53.160 --> 05:54.850
70 million

05:54.430 --> 06:03.800
-70 million

05:54.430 --> 06:03.800
-70 million

05:54.850 --> 06:00.100
70 million

05:54.850 --> 06:00.100
70 million

05:56.690 --> 05:59.290
we can pay you what we promised,

05:59.290 --> 06:01.320
and we won't be penalized.

06:00.100 --> 06:03.800
70 million

06:00.100 --> 06:03.800
70 million

06:01.320 --> 06:03.800
This makes the result for us three...

06:05.490 --> 06:07.820
It's a win-win-win!

06:07.820 --> 06:10.590
So the 70 million is basically free?!

06:12.000 --> 06:13.230
Crazy how that works out.

06:13.230 --> 06:15.470
So, what'll it be?

06:15.820 --> 06:18.340
We'll gladly buy the votes!

06:18.340 --> 06:20.850
Thing is, I can only sell you two each.

06:20.850 --> 06:22.230
Two votes?!

06:22.910 --> 06:24.980
Those are a big two votes.

06:24.980 --> 06:28.680
They'll get you both out of last place.

06:30.130 --> 06:32.380
You don't have to buy 
if you don't want to.

06:32.840 --> 06:36.680
But if you don't, one of the 
two of you is going down.

06:36.680 --> 06:37.730
That's all there is to it.

06:37.730 --> 06:38.720
We'll buy!

06:38.720 --> 06:40.430
We'll do it, okay?

06:42.400 --> 06:44.160
Hey, Fukunaga.

06:44.160 --> 06:48.140
Kitamura and Eda just bought 
two votes each for 70 million.

06:48.410 --> 06:51.310
That puts you in last place 
by your lonesome.

06:52.460 --> 06:54.520
I'll sell you some votes if you'd like.

06:54.870 --> 06:59.400
But for you, two votes will be 80 million.

07:01.400 --> 07:11.430
Nao Kanzaki



 Tetsuzo Sato


 Takayoshi Miura



 Shingo Fujita


 Takahiro Kikuzawa



 Kosuke Tsunoda

07:01.400 --> 07:11.780
Teruyuki Eda



 Hiroto Kitamura


 Yuji Fukunaga

07:01.940 --> 07:05.290
Fukunaga-san bought two votes immediately.

07:05.780 --> 07:10.900
The purchases by our three buyers
left the other five tied for last place.

07:11.780 --> 07:12.800
Teruyuki Eda



 Hiroto Kitamura


 Yuji Fukunaga

07:12.680 --> 07:15.600
Nao Kanzaki


 Teruyuki Eda



Hiroto Kitamura


 Yuji Fukunaga

07:12.680 --> 07:17.290
Tetsuzo Sato



 Takayoshi Miura


 Shingo Fujita


 Takahiro Kikuzawa



 Kosuke Tsunoda

07:13.200 --> 07:16.840
Naturally, the five of them
 sprang into action.

07:17.620 --> 07:19.400
It's 100 million yen for two votes.

07:19.790 --> 07:22.410
A-A hundred million?!

07:22.410 --> 07:24.730
You don't have to buy 
if you don't want to.

07:24.730 --> 07:26.960
Have fun losing, though.

07:29.400 --> 07:30.420
Sold!

07:30.760 --> 07:32.280
The votes went.

07:32.860 --> 07:36.030
I'd originally bought lots 
of ten votes for 70 million,

07:36.030 --> 07:39.110
a cost of seven million per vote.

07:39.810 --> 07:42.470
Now we were selling two for 100 million.

07:40.930 --> 07:43.940
Transaction with: Nao Kanzaki

07:40.930 --> 07:43.940
Takahiro Kikuzawa

07:40.930 --> 07:43.940
Terms: Buy two votes 
from Nao Kanzaki

07:40.930 --> 07:43.940
Amount

07:43.030 --> 07:45.440
In other words, 50 million per vote.

07:46.200 --> 07:49.560
A roughly sevenfold increase in price.

07:51.440 --> 07:54.630
Akiyama-san continued 
his brazen behavior.

07:55.760 --> 07:58.930
Everyone else has now bought two votes,

07:58.930 --> 08:01.600
which puts you guys back at the bottom.

08:01.600 --> 08:03.780
Well? Wanna buy more?

08:03.780 --> 08:05.020
Yes, please.

08:05.020 --> 08:07.500
That'll be 50 million per vote.

08:07.500 --> 08:09.640
Fifty million?!

08:09.640 --> 08:12.000
Or you can buy two 
for a special discount:

08:12.000 --> 08:13.850
just 95 million.

08:13.850 --> 08:15.930
Ninety-five million?!

08:15.930 --> 08:18.090
That's all the money we have left!

08:18.430 --> 08:21.860
Well, I was selling votes to the 
last group at 50 million a pop.

08:21.860 --> 08:25.170
I can't exactly go giving 
you guys special treatment.

08:27.830 --> 08:30.240
We'll buy the two votes.

08:30.720 --> 08:32.900
It was close to 50 million a vote,

08:33.590 --> 08:35.360
and yet they still bought them.

08:35.710 --> 08:40.350
But of course, not everyone took
 the extortion lying down.

08:42.550 --> 08:44.620
I just came up with a foolproof plan!

08:44.620 --> 08:47.370
I don't want to lose for not buying votes.

08:47.370 --> 08:49.670
But I don't wanna pay out 
the nose for them, either.

08:50.630 --> 08:54.880
So I'll sell off my own votes and lose!

08:55.220 --> 08:58.500
They were just selling votes 
for 50 million apiece.

08:58.500 --> 09:01.550
I'll sell my own for half that!

09:01.550 --> 09:04.970
I've only got 65 million right now.

09:04.970 --> 09:07.580
If I sell two votes to three 
people for 25 million each,

09:07.580 --> 09:10.900
I'll wind up with 215 million!

09:10.900 --> 09:14.550
215 million

09:10.900 --> 09:13.550
I'll be the loser, to be sure,

09:13.960 --> 09:15.670
but I'll pay the 100 mil for this game

09:14.050 --> 09:16.680
115 million

09:14.170 --> 09:15.070
100 million

09:15.670 --> 09:18.130
plus the 100 million I owe
 from the last one,

09:16.400 --> 09:20.930
15 million

09:16.430 --> 09:17.680
100 million

09:18.130 --> 09:20.900
and I'll still walk away with 15 million!

09:21.330 --> 09:25.170
It's perfect! A surefire way out!

09:25.530 --> 09:30.000
Meanwhile, Akiyama-san raised 
the price of our votes again.

09:31.200 --> 09:33.660
It's 65 million per vote.

09:34.040 --> 09:36.290
Sixty-five million?!

09:36.290 --> 09:40.250
Th-That's all the money I have...

09:40.250 --> 09:45.090
Seems like it's worth the price to me.

09:48.340 --> 09:50.180
Give me time to think.

09:50.600 --> 09:52.490
I'll be back in three minutes.

09:54.950 --> 09:56.630
Now's my chance!

09:58.720 --> 09:59.770
What?

09:59.770 --> 10:02.370
Akiyama's really gouging us, right?

10:02.370 --> 10:04.610
I'll sell you my votes for 
half what he's charging.

10:04.610 --> 10:06.450
For real? You're cool with that?

10:06.450 --> 10:09.880
Some stuff happened, and I wound 
up with more votes than I need.

10:10.150 --> 10:12.890
I'll sell you a few out of 
the goodness of my heart.

10:13.630 --> 10:14.630
Transaction with: Kosuke Tsunoda

10:13.630 --> 10:14.630
Tetsuzo Sato

10:13.630 --> 10:14.630
Terms:Sell two votes 
to Kosuke Tsunoda

10:13.630 --> 10:14.630
Amount

10:15.460 --> 10:17.400
You're a lifesaver!

10:17.400 --> 10:19.370
I owe you, man!

10:19.680 --> 10:23.160
He agreed to it just like that!

10:23.160 --> 10:26.780
Now let's see if I can get 
two more people!

10:27.130 --> 10:28.400
No, thank you.

10:28.400 --> 10:29.650
Screw that.

10:29.650 --> 10:31.400
No way, man.

10:31.400 --> 10:33.050
H-How come?

10:33.050 --> 10:34.210
Too expensive?

10:34.210 --> 10:38.030
I can do two votes for 40...
 No, 30 million!

10:39.040 --> 10:41.480
You're aiming to lose, right?

10:43.240 --> 10:47.870
We all know you sold votes to 
Tsunoda with the goal of losing.

10:47.870 --> 10:50.740
That puts you at the bottom right now.

10:50.740 --> 10:54.820
The rest of us don't even need 
to buy votes to survive.

10:56.670 --> 11:00.540
The person who figured out 
Sato-san was trying to lose

11:00.540 --> 11:04.540
and leaked that to the other 
players was Akiyama-san.

11:05.400 --> 11:09.630
Sato-san ended up coming 
back to Akiyama-san.

11:09.630 --> 11:14.020
I'll take as many votes as my 
remaining money can buy, please.

11:16.930 --> 11:21.350
Sato-san's purchase made the state 
of last place opaque once more,

11:21.350 --> 11:23.800
and the buying of votes resumed.

11:24.550 --> 11:27.810
Akiyama-san had everyone
in the palm of his hand.

11:28.650 --> 11:32.420
He was truly the one
 in control of the game.

11:32.420 --> 11:39.170
Transaction with: Nao Kanzaki

11:32.420 --> 11:39.170
Teruyuki Eda

11:32.420 --> 11:39.170
Terms: Buy two votes 
from Nao Kanzaki

11:32.420 --> 11:39.170
Amount

11:33.230 --> 11:35.150
That's 900 million.

11:35.150 --> 11:38.660
The game money of everyone 
here now belongs to you.

11:39.160 --> 11:40.710
Incredible.

11:40.710 --> 11:43.650
And we're the only ones who know...

11:45.230 --> 11:48.690
who will rise to the top
 and who's going down.

11:48.680 --> 11:53.020
Nao Kanzaki

11:53.890 --> 11:57.270
We will now begin the final vote.

11:57.610 --> 12:00.190
The game's ending at last.

12:01.360 --> 12:05.160
I wonder who will come out the loser.

12:07.560 --> 12:10.260
You must all be quite on edge.

12:10.260 --> 12:13.550
You spent all the money 
you had buying votes,

12:13.550 --> 12:17.480
but most of you haven't secured the
fifty you need to ensure victory.

12:18.470 --> 12:22.480
You still have a chance to 
make a comeback, though.

12:23.660 --> 12:27.550
Nao still has her five 
final votes to cast.

12:27.550 --> 12:29.800
She hasn't yet decided who gets them.

12:30.120 --> 12:33.340
Not even I know how things will turn out.

12:33.950 --> 12:37.990
The allocation of those five 
votes is 100% up to her.

12:39.420 --> 12:41.590
Don't think of them as just five votes.

12:41.590 --> 12:45.540
Those five votes could save 
someone from the bottom

12:45.540 --> 12:47.940
or sink someone who 
thought they were safe.

12:48.920 --> 12:51.330
It's time to make your pitches to her.

12:51.330 --> 12:53.130
And you'd better make them good.

12:53.660 --> 12:56.150
Explain to her why she should save you.

12:56.580 --> 12:59.260
Nao, you have my word!

12:59.260 --> 13:04.170
If you save me now, 
I'll always help you from now on!

13:04.170 --> 13:07.220
You'll definitely be better off
 with me on your side!

13:07.220 --> 13:09.940
That's bull, Fukunaga.

13:09.940 --> 13:12.460
No one here can trust you!

13:12.460 --> 13:15.470
Besides, Nao-chan's got
 a ton of money right now.

13:15.750 --> 13:17.530
She's obviously gonna drop out.

13:18.420 --> 13:20.020
Save me, then!

13:20.020 --> 13:23.690
If I fall any further into debt,
I might be killed!

13:23.690 --> 13:25.210
I-I'm in the same boat!

13:25.210 --> 13:28.040
There are some really scary 
people who might kill me!

13:28.040 --> 13:28.720
Same here!

13:28.720 --> 13:29.450
Me, too!

13:29.820 --> 13:33.590
Maybe trash like you is better off dead.

13:33.590 --> 13:34.340
What?!

13:35.810 --> 13:36.700
Damn you!

13:36.700 --> 13:38.410
You wanna do this?!

13:43.430 --> 13:45.080
Stop it!

13:45.080 --> 13:48.600
I don't want to hear a single 
thing from any of you!

13:50.490 --> 13:52.720
You're all so self-serving.

13:52.720 --> 13:58.650
Not one of you heard me out 
during the first pitch meeting.

14:00.460 --> 14:04.350
I already know how I'm voting.

14:05.120 --> 14:06.920
I've filled out all the names.

14:16.540 --> 14:17.870
You heard her.

14:18.470 --> 14:20.400
So it's all over now.

14:20.800 --> 14:25.430
All you can do is accept 
the results as they come.

14:28.580 --> 14:31.630
It is now time to reveal the votes.

14:31.630 --> 14:34.460
There has been significant 
movement in vote tallies,

14:34.460 --> 14:37.910
but as this is the last vote, 
only the final result matters.

14:37.910 --> 14:41.140
I will therefore announce the totals
 starting from first place.

14:42.400 --> 14:44.150
First place:

14:45.170 --> 14:46.900
Nao Kanzaki

14:45.430 --> 14:46.900
Nao Kanzaki.

14:46.900 --> 14:49.010
Fifty-one votes?

14:49.010 --> 14:52.040
If she alone took first 
place with 51 votes,

14:52.040 --> 14:54.060
then last place will have 49?

14:54.750 --> 14:57.240
The following were tied.

14:59.250 --> 15:03.750
Nao Kanzaki

14:59.690 --> 15:01.190
In second place:

15:01.750 --> 15:03.750
Kosuke Tsunoda

15:01.970 --> 15:03.760
Kosuke Tsunoda.

15:05.390 --> 15:10.270
I actually made it to 
fifty votes all by myself.

15:10.260 --> 15:14.010
Nao Kanzaki

15:10.260 --> 15:14.010
Kosuke Tsunoda

15:10.640 --> 15:12.040
Also in second place:

15:12.260 --> 15:14.010
Teruyuki Eda

15:12.480 --> 15:14.000
Teruyuki Eda.

15:14.420 --> 15:16.510
For real? Awesome!

15:16.840 --> 15:18.300
Also in second place:

15:18.300 --> 15:19.720
Shingo Fujita.

15:19.720 --> 15:21.010
Yes!

15:21.340 --> 15:22.730
Also in second place:

15:22.730 --> 15:24.350
Takahiro Kikuzawa.

15:24.350 --> 15:26.140
Hell yeah!

15:26.480 --> 15:28.120
Also in second place:

15:28.120 --> 15:29.470
Hiroto Kitamura.

15:29.470 --> 15:30.650
Yes!

15:32.980 --> 15:35.400
Three people left.

15:35.980 --> 15:37.290
Let's see...

15:37.910 --> 15:40.610
Who will the loser be?

15:42.830 --> 15:44.540
I know who it is.

15:44.820 --> 15:47.030
Sato's going to be the loser.

15:47.030 --> 15:51.110
He tried to take the money 
and bail, but he failed.

15:51.540 --> 15:56.800
I saw him go crying to Akiyama, but at 
those prices, he could only buy two votes.

15:57.170 --> 16:02.320
Unless Nao gave him all her votes 
at the end, he's going to be the loser.

16:02.560 --> 16:04.050
Also in second place...

16:04.050 --> 16:05.830
Say it.

16:05.830 --> 16:07.600
Say my name!

16:10.280 --> 16:11.820
Tetsuzo Sato.

16:12.110 --> 16:13.140
What?!

16:14.330 --> 16:15.760
How?!

16:15.760 --> 16:19.500
Nao, don't tell me you voted
for him at the end!

16:19.500 --> 16:20.460
Oh, no.

16:20.760 --> 16:23.960
I didn't cast a single vote for Sato-san.

16:23.960 --> 16:24.970
Huh?

16:25.610 --> 16:27.920
Nao Kanzaki didn't have to vote for him.

16:28.910 --> 16:33.970
When Sato came to us asking for all 
the votes his money would buy,

16:33.970 --> 16:37.490
I sold him enough to get him 
to the fifty-vote safe zone.

16:37.840 --> 16:42.580
So he knew he'd won before 
the announcement began.

16:47.100 --> 16:49.110
Akiyama tricked me!

16:49.430 --> 16:53.770
That bastard had it out 
for me from the start!

16:54.300 --> 16:57.300
One player remains tied for second.

16:57.300 --> 17:00.060
The player whose name is 
not called is in last place.

17:00.060 --> 17:02.020
In other words, they are the loser.

17:02.020 --> 17:03.750
I will now make the announcement.

17:03.750 --> 17:07.260
Damn it, damn it... Damn it!

17:07.250 --> 17:12.010
Takahiro Kikuzawa



 Hiroto Kitamura



 Tetsuzo Sato

17:07.260 --> 17:09.740
The final player tied for second:

17:10.470 --> 17:12.000
Yuji Fukunaga.

17:10.500 --> 17:12.010
Yuji Fukunaga

17:12.420 --> 17:13.280
Huh?

17:13.280 --> 17:16.750
Yes! I won!

17:16.750 --> 17:20.260
Thank you, Nao! Thank you so much!

17:21.080 --> 17:22.590
I lost...

17:22.590 --> 17:23.790
But why?

17:24.540 --> 17:25.850
Why me?

17:27.610 --> 17:29.480
Let me explain.

17:29.890 --> 17:36.540
As I said before, nobody heard 
me out during the pitch meeting.

17:37.200 --> 17:41.860
And after that, everyone else
 completely ignored me.

17:42.360 --> 17:47.370
When I was drowning in despair, you were 
the only one who reached out to me.

17:47.370 --> 17:51.630
And you said you were sorry 
you couldn't save me.

17:52.200 --> 17:53.490
That made me so happy.

17:53.790 --> 17:56.890
Then why did you make me the loser?!

17:57.640 --> 18:02.380
I've come up with a surefire plan
 to beat the Liar Game.

18:02.660 --> 18:04.280
What?

18:04.280 --> 18:10.070
In the Liar Game, as long as nobody 
tries to take the money for themselves,

18:10.070 --> 18:11.670
it's possible to save everyone.

18:12.340 --> 18:16.570
In each game so far, the LGT Office 
has lent participants 100 million,

18:16.570 --> 18:20.160
and when the game is over, 
they take that money back.

18:20.160 --> 18:24.330
Which means, as long as 
the winner doesn't drop out,

18:24.330 --> 18:26.940
the LGT Office doesn't make any money.

18:26.940 --> 18:30.930
By the same token, as a group, 
the players don't lose anything.

18:31.240 --> 18:33.010
For instance, in the first round,

18:33.010 --> 18:35.710
if neither player took from 
the other's 100 million,

18:35.710 --> 18:37.740
neither would be out anything.

18:38.670 --> 18:42.570
Same for the second game. 
The rules stated it was winner takes all,

18:42.570 --> 18:46.360
but if they redistributed 
their winnings to the others,

18:46.360 --> 18:50.430
everyone else would 
have been free and clear.

18:50.690 --> 18:53.180
But the winner would still 
be stuck in the game!

18:53.180 --> 18:54.350
No.

18:54.350 --> 18:57.920
The winners just have to keep doing 
the same thing as they advance.

18:58.350 --> 19:01.930
As the tournament goes on, 
there will be fewer and fewer winners.

19:01.930 --> 19:04.050
In the end, everyone can get out.

19:05.370 --> 19:08.870
Typical of someone so stupidly honest. 
Just a moronic abstract theory.

19:09.440 --> 19:10.570
Do you think so?

19:11.430 --> 19:15.550
I feel like it tells me what the 
LGT Office is really after.

19:16.110 --> 19:20.300
The only way they make money is 
when they can make players drop out.

19:20.750 --> 19:26.390
When one person lies, tricks others
 to serve their own greed,

19:26.390 --> 19:29.020
makes money, and drops out...

19:29.020 --> 19:31.610
That's the only time the 
LGT Office makes money.

19:32.050 --> 19:35.220
So whenever the LGT Office turns a profit,

19:35.220 --> 19:38.550
it means there were players
 who went unsaved.

19:40.290 --> 19:46.400
Do you all think the Liar Game 
is a game where liars win?

19:47.680 --> 19:49.640
I don't think it is.

19:50.230 --> 19:52.770
What I think the Liar Game
 is really about...

19:53.330 --> 19:58.880
is testing your ability to beat the 
temptation to make yourself a liar.

19:58.880 --> 20:01.240
Your ability to remain honest.

20:03.040 --> 20:06.880
In today's Downsizing Game, if you put 
yourself in the shoes of the liar,

20:06.880 --> 20:11.600
here's how it plays: "It's a game 
about taking one idiot down."

20:13.310 --> 20:17.990
But from the perspective of an 
honest person, it goes like this:

20:18.420 --> 20:21.330
"It's a game where we 
can save one person."

20:23.220 --> 20:27.170
Of course, I think the latter is 
the real meaning of the game.

20:27.750 --> 20:28.700
And so...

20:29.620 --> 20:31.780
I'm saving Miura-san.

20:34.480 --> 20:35.880
Take this.

20:36.430 --> 20:38.820
It's an M Ticket worth 200 million yen.

20:39.120 --> 20:41.620
It will cover the 100-million 
entry fee for this game,

20:39.130 --> 20:49.640
Transaction with: Takayoshi Miura

20:39.130 --> 20:49.640
Nao Kanzaki

20:39.130 --> 20:49.640
Amount

20:41.620 --> 20:44.670
plus your 100-million debt 
from the last game.

20:45.180 --> 20:49.640
Which means you're now free
 from the Liar Game.

20:51.220 --> 20:52.680
Nao-chan...

21:00.070 --> 21:05.160
Miura-san was the only person here
 who was honest with me.

21:05.580 --> 21:10.240
That's why I'm saving him 
by making him the loser.

21:13.160 --> 21:18.550
I'm currently holding 
 all of your money as well,

21:18.950 --> 21:22.180
and I'll be returning it to each of you.

21:22.970 --> 21:25.630
None of you will lose 
anything in this game.

21:25.630 --> 21:29.920
You can all enter the third game 
just as you ended the second.

21:29.920 --> 21:32.910
Yeah!

21:32.910 --> 21:36.440
And so the Losers' Revival Match
 came to a close.

21:36.990 --> 21:40.520
Miura-san exited the Liar Game
 free and clear,

21:40.520 --> 21:44.430
and the rest could move on to the 
third-round game in the same state

21:44.430 --> 21:46.540
they were in before it began.

21:48.470 --> 21:50.220
Nao Kanzaki...

21:51.310 --> 21:53.650
What an interesting girl.

21:54.440 --> 21:57.570
I thought she was the 
stupidest person there,

21:57.570 --> 22:00.710
but she seems sharper than I thought.

22:00.710 --> 22:02.280
Leronira-san...

22:04.290 --> 22:06.210
That's fine by me.

22:07.030 --> 22:12.840
The tournament is about 
to get very entertaining.

23:45.060 --> 23:50.060
Next Time

23:45.060 --> 23:50.060
Contraband Game
